%N A402373 Decimal expansion of 27*A/38, where A is Artin's constant (A005596): the conjectured relative density of the primes having a Fibonacci primitive root.
%C A402373 A Fibonacci primitive root modulo a prime p is a primitive root g modulo p such that g^2 == g + 1 (mod p) (see A003147).
%C A402373 Shanks (1972) conjectured that the number of primes p <= x having a Fibonacci primitive root is asymptotic to this constant times the number of primes p <= x. Sander (1990) proved this under the assumption of the Riemann hypothesis for the fields Q(phi^(1/k), zeta_(2k)), k >= 1, where phi = (1+sqrt(5))/2 and zeta_(2k) is a primitive (2k)-th root of unity.
%C A402373 Among the 455052511 primes below 10^10, exactly 120907765 have a Fibonacci primitive root, a proportion of 0.2657006... (see A398918).
%H A402373 J. W. Sander, <a href="https://www.fq.math.ca/Scanned/28-1/sander.pdf">On Fibonacci primitive roots</a>, Fibonacci Quarterly, Vol. 28, No. 1 (1990), pp. 79-80.
%H A402373 Daniel Shanks, <a href="https://www.fq.math.ca/Scanned/10-2/shanks-a.pdf">Fibonacci primitive roots</a>, <a href="https://www.fq.math.ca/Scanned/10-2/shanks-b.pdf">end of article</a>, Fibonacci Quarterly, Vol. 10, No. 2 (1972), pp. 163-168, 181.
%F A402373 Equals (27/38)*Product_{p prime} (1 - 1/(p*(p-1))) = 27*A005596/38.
%e A402373 0.26570544651890688888099098598298008442142078190436976675152778066495933987054626903411...
%o A402373 (PARI) default(realprecision, 110); 27/38*prodeulerrat(1 - 1/(p^2-p))
